{
  "_comment": [
    "THE DIGEST OF EVERY CONTRACT VERSION THIS ENGINE HOLDS, RECORDED ONCE.",
    "",
    "A version is a promise about a shape. Editing the file without moving",
    "the $id keeps the promise's name and changes what it promises, and the",
    "consumer that already declared support carries on saying so while",
    "reading something else. Nothing in the tree can tell that apart from a",
    "correct edit: both are a changed file. This ledger is what tells them",
    "apart, because it was written when the version was.",
    "",
    "IT FOUND THREE. `collection/1.0.0` gained a required property and",
    "repointed two references, `comparison/3.0.0` repointed two, and",
    "`evidence/3.0.0` gained two properties, all after v1.0.0b6 published",
    "them and all under the identity that was published. The versions the",
    "cascade did move -- run, run-set, assessment to 4.1.0 -- were moved by",
    "hand, and by hand is exactly how the other three were missed.",
    "",
    "ADDING A LINE IS THE DELIBERATE ACT. A new version arrives with a new",
    "digest and a new line, reviewed beside the schema that produced it.",
    "Changing a line is almost always the defect this file exists to catch;",
    "the exception is a version that has never been published, and that is",
    "an argument to make in review rather than an edit to make quietly."
  ],
